# yard.epic: the flow of rig yard's epics (yardr rig flow yard --type epic
# yard.epic). An epic waits in open while its children are open (each child
# blocks it); once the last closes, yard-integrators rebases its branch onto
# main and gates it, Codex reviews the whole diff, and the refinery lands it
# on main as one fast-forward. See docs/pipeline.md#epics.
backlog -> open
open -> review on done | open on failed | backlog
review -> approved on done | open on changes | decide on question
approved -> merged on done | open on failed | merge on conflict
merge -> review on done | open on rework | decide on question
decide -> open | backlog
merged terminal
